space_Veins smoke tests. Please ignore.

To run this simulation, execute the script `sim/space_veins_testsims/space_veins_test/runall`.

This simulation requires sumo-launchd to be started and listening for
connections on a TCP socket, e.g. using "~/lib/veins/src/veins/bin/veins_launchd -vv".

This test compares satellite position updates with those from a backup.

Setup:
- 1 satellite
- a backup `.csv` file containing all the satellite position updates from a previous run. (See below for instructions on how to create a new one.)

Functionality:
- values from the `.csv` file will be pushed into a std::vector
- after each satellite position update, the new coordinates are compared with those in the vector. Afterwards, they are removed from the vector

The test will fail if the comparison does not match (be aware of assertClose, because of floating-point operations), or if the size of the vector does not match.

`validateSatPos.csv` contains omnetCoords to validate the current SatelliteMobility.

## Create a new `.csv` file:
1. run test module `./runall` -> in `results/` a new `.vec` file will be created
2. run `script/createNewCsv.sh`
3. run `mv script/newValidateSatPos.csv ./validateSatPos.csv`
